a number called gen_instances is 0.

a number called gen_values is 0.

(The `value` type: declare, print, reassign across the type boundary
 (number to text), print again - the exact round-trip that produced
 compiler bugs #2, #8 and #15 (finding 06). Runtime-tag ABI.)

To 'gen leaf value roundtrip' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    Set gen_values to gen_values add 1.
    a text called 'starting number' is 'literal integer'.
    a text called decl is "a value called y{gen_values} is {'starting number'}".
    a text called 'print number' is "Print y{gen_values}".
    a text called reassign is "Set y{gen_values} to \"reassigned{gen_values}\"".
    a text called 'print text' is "Print y{gen_values}".
    a list called 'the lines' is [decl, 'print number', reassign, 'print text'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(Thing member functions: this leaf drives both call forms - the
 type-possessive maker (`a <type>'s <maker> with ...`, the only way to
 reach a member whose first parameter is not the thing,
 LANGUAGE.md:1600) and the instance-possessive receiver
 (`i's <receiver>`, LANGUAGE.md:1539) - and reads the owner-return field
 back after each (finding 03). Data fields alone cannot reach the
 dispatch and owner-return path.

 It needs a thing that has BOTH kinds of member and a number field for
 them to write, and no rule says a program has one, so it asks the
 manifest and stands aside when this program's prelude has none. The
 field it prints is the one the manifest recorded the method as writing,
 so the print shows what the call put there.)

To 'gen leaf thing member' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a boolean called 'a thing is available' is 'gen manifest pick a thing with both members'.
    If 'a thing is available' is false then,
        'gen leaf thing copy' of indent and nested,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a number called 'the thing' is gen_pick_thing.
    a number called 'the maker' is gen_pick_maker.
    a number called 'the receiver' is gen_pick_receiver.
    a text called 'the type' is 'gen thing written' of 'the thing'.
    a text called 'the type possessive' is 'gen thing possessive' of 'the thing'.
    a text called 'the maker name' is 'gen method written' of 'the maker'.
    a text called 'the receiver name' is 'gen method written' of 'the receiver'.
    a number called 'the maker field' is element 'the maker' of gen_method_field.
    a number called 'the receiver field' is element 'the receiver' of gen_method_field.
    a text called 'the maker field name' is 'gen field written' of 'the maker field'.
    a text called 'the receiver field name' is 'gen field written' of 'the receiver field'.
    Set gen_instances to gen_instances add 1.
    a number called 'maker name' is gen_instances.
    a text called 'starting value' is 'literal integer'.
    Set gen_instances to gen_instances add 1.
    a number called 'mirror name' is gen_instances.
    a text called decl is "a {'the type'} called i{'maker name'} is a {'the type possessive'} {'the maker name'} with {'starting value'}".
    a text called 'print maker' is "Print i{'maker name'}'s {'the maker field name'}".
    a text called 'mirror decl' is "a {'the type'} called i{'mirror name'} is i{'maker name'}'s {'the receiver name'}".
    a text called 'print mirror' is "Print i{'mirror name'}'s {'the receiver field name'}".
    a list called 'the lines' is [decl, 'print maker', 'mirror decl', 'print mirror'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(Things: instance declaration, possessive field read/write, and
 whole-thing printing. The flat form wants any thing with a number
 field; the nested form wants a thing whose field is a thing that has
 one, so the chained possessive `i's <outer>'s <inner>` has something to
 read. Neither shape is guaranteed - the old prelude guaranteed both
 with t1/t2 and t3, which is precisely the sameness this replaces - so
 each asks first.)

To 'gen thing flat' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a boolean called 'a thing is available' is 'gen manifest pick a plain thing'.
    If 'a thing is available' is false then,
        'gen manifest stand aside' of indent and nested,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a text called 'the type' is 'gen thing written' of gen_pick_thing.
    a text called 'the field' is 'gen field written' of gen_pick_field.
    Set gen_instances to gen_instances add 1.
    a text called val is 'literal integer'.
    a text called decl is "a {'the type'} called i{gen_instances}".
    a text called 'set line' is "Set i{gen_instances}'s {'the field'} to {val}".
    a text called 'print line' is "Print i{gen_instances}".
    a list called 'the lines' is [decl, 'set line', 'print line'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

To 'gen thing nested' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a boolean called 'a nesting is available' is 'gen manifest pick a nested thing'.
    If 'a nesting is available' is false then,
        'gen thing flat' of indent and nested,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a text called 'the type' is 'gen thing written' of gen_pick_thing.
    (The outer field is written as a POSSESSIVE and the inner as a plain
     name: `i1's 'the inner mark's 'the north offset'`, one apostrophe
     between them, never two. Hand-verified against 0.4.7.)
    a text called 'the outer' is 'gen field possessive' of gen_pick_field.
    a text called 'the inner' is 'gen field written' of gen_pick_inner_field.
    Set gen_instances to gen_instances add 1.
    a text called val is 'literal integer'.
    a text called decl is "a {'the type'} called i{gen_instances}".
    a text called 'set line' is "Set i{gen_instances}'s {'the outer'} {'the inner'} to {val}".
    a text called 'field line' is "Print i{gen_instances}'s {'the outer'} {'the inner'}".
    a text called 'whole line' is "Print i{gen_instances}".
    a list called 'the lines' is [decl, 'set line', 'field line', 'whole line'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(Drawn through a PRIME modulus, not `'rng below' of 2`. This LCG's low
 bits are correlated - the hazard is documented above 'gen leaf loop
 control' - and the flat/nested coin was locked by it: measured over 150
 programs on main, `a t3 called i#` appeared in ZERO of them, so the
 nested leaf had never once run in a campaign. `r modulo 11` depends on
 the whole of r rather than its bottom bit.)

To 'gen leaf thing' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a number called 'the kind draw' is 'rng below' of 11.
    If 'the kind draw' is less than 5 then,
        'gen thing flat' of indent and nested,
        Return a boolean, false.
    'gen thing nested' of indent and nested.

(Value-copy check: assign one instance to another, mutate the copy,
 and print both fields back out - the two must differ, proving the
 copy shares nothing with the original.)

To 'gen leaf thing copy' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a boolean called 'a thing is available' is 'gen manifest pick a plain thing'.
    If 'a thing is available' is false then,
        'gen manifest stand aside' of indent and nested,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a text called 'the type' is 'gen thing written' of gen_pick_thing.
    a text called 'the field' is 'gen field written' of gen_pick_field.
    Set gen_instances to gen_instances add 1.
    a number called 'original name' is gen_instances.
    a text called val is 'literal integer'.
    Set gen_instances to gen_instances add 1.
    a number called 'copy name' is gen_instances.
    a text called val2 is 'literal integer'.
    a text called decl is "a {'the type'} called i{'original name'}".
    a text called 'set line' is "Set i{'original name'}'s {'the field'} to {val}".
    a text called 'copy decl' is "a {'the type'} called i{'copy name'} is i{'original name'}".
    a text called 'mutate line' is "Set i{'copy name'}'s {'the field'} to {val2}".
    a text called 'print orig' is "Print i{'original name'}'s {'the field'}".
    a text called 'print copy' is "Print i{'copy name'}'s {'the field'}".
    a list called 'the lines' is [decl, 'set line', 'copy decl', 'mutate line', 'print orig', 'print copy'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(--- the things block ---

 Emitted once per program, before the statement stream that uses it.
 Everything here reads the manifest; nothing decides anything, which is
 what makes the definitions and the leaves agree.

 What pins the order, and all that does:

 - A nested field's type must be a PREVIOUSLY DEFINED thing
   (LANGUAGE.md:994), so the definitions go out in manifest order, which
   is the order they were built in and therefore the order in which a
   nesting target always precedes the field that nests it. Which thing
   nests which IS drawn, so the dependency structure varies even though
   the traversal does not.
 - A member definition names its owner type (LANGUAGE.md:1426), so a
   thing's methods follow its definition.

 Nothing pins whether the methods follow IMMEDIATELY. Hand-verified
 against 0.4.7 both ways: all the definitions and then all the methods
 compiles, and each definition followed by its own methods compiles.
 So which of the two a program gets is drawn - and the fifteen-line
 t3-to-mirrored block that `scripts/invariants` reported as "always
 contiguous and in this order" in 150 of 150 programs has nothing left
 to be contiguous about.)

(THG2-70's dispatch function has no thing to depend on, so it is built
 first, unconditionally - even a program with zero things gets one, on
 the same "drawn whether or not it is used" rule 'gen build manifest
 extras' already follows for the grid sink and the flag reader, so the
 seed-to-name mapping never depends on a decision taken elsewhere.

 THG2-21/27/30/32's pair, by contrast, names a thing type in its own
 signature, so it can only be built once that type is on the page - the
 call sites below run AFTER either emission path, never before.)

To 'gen emit things block'.
    'gen build thing predicate function'.
    (Reset here, unconditionally, rather than only inside 'gen build
     thing functions' - one process generates many programs in a loop,
     reusing every global, and a program with zero things returns below
     before that function is ever called. Without this reset a THING-
     FREE program inherited gen_thing_function_ready true (and a stale owner/
     field pair) from whichever earlier program in the same run last set
     it, and 'gen leaf thing free function' and friends fired on a thing
     that was never declared - hand-caught: seed 111 of a 200-program
     run emitted `a  called i1.` and called a function taking it, both
     with an EMPTY type name, because program 111 has no things at all.)
    Set gen_thing_function_ready to false.
    Set gen_thing_function_nested_ready to false.
    a number called 'how many things' is gen_thing_names's length.
    If 'how many things' is 0 then,
        Return a number, 0.
    a number called 'the grouping draw' is 'rng below' of 11.
    If 'the grouping draw' is less than 5 then,
        'gen emit things grouped' of 'how many things',
        'gen build thing functions',
        Return a number, 0.
    'gen emit things interleaved' of 'how many things'.
    'gen build thing functions'.
    Return a number, 0.

To 'gen emit things grouped' with a number called 'how many things'.
    a number called 'the thing' is 1.
    While 'the thing' is less than or equal to 'how many things',
        'gen emit one thing definition' of 'the thing',
        Set 'the thing' to 'the thing' add 1.
    a number called 'the owner' is 1.
    While 'the owner' is less than or equal to 'how many things',
        'gen emit methods of' of 'the owner',
        Set 'the owner' to 'the owner' add 1.
    Return a number, 0.

To 'gen emit things interleaved' with a number called 'how many things'.
    a number called 'the thing' is 1.
    While 'the thing' is less than or equal to 'how many things',
        'gen emit one thing definition' of 'the thing',
        'gen emit methods of' of 'the thing',
        Set 'the thing' to 'the thing' add 1.
    Return a number, 0.

(One definition. Data fields and manifest entries may appear in any
 order inside the body - hand-verified against 0.4.7 with a function
 member between two data fields - so the two runs are shuffled together
 by a drawn interleave rather than emitted methods-first the way the old
 template did.

 The last entry ends with a period and every earlier one with a comma,
 which is the language's own list punctuation (LANGUAGE.md:952-954), and
 the blank line after the body is what closes it (LANGUAGE.md:81-87).)

To 'gen emit one thing definition' with a number called 'the thing'.
    a text called 'the type' is 'gen thing written' of 'the thing'.
    'gen emit' of "A thing called {'the type'} has\n".
    a number called 'the first field' is element 'the thing' of gen_thing_field_first.
    a number called 'how many fields' is element 'the thing' of gen_thing_field_count.
    a number called 'the first method' is element 'the thing' of gen_thing_method_first.
    a number called 'how many methods' is element 'the thing' of gen_thing_method_count.
    a number called 'the fields left' is 'how many fields'.
    a number called 'the methods left' is 'how many methods'.
    a number called 'the field step' is 0.
    a number called 'the method step' is 0.
    a number called 'how many entries' is 'how many fields' add 'how many methods'.
    a number called 'the entries written' is 0.
    (The increment is the loop's LAST plain statement, so its period
     closes the loop - language note 6b. An earlier draft ended the body
     on an If instead, which left the loop open and swallowed the
     paragraph break that closes the thing: every entry came out
     followed by a blank line, and a blank line closes the body
     (LANGUAGE.md:81-87).)
    While 'the entries written' is less than 'how many entries',
        a number called 'the choice' is 'rng below' of 13,
        a boolean called 'write a method here' is false,
        If 'the methods left' is greater than 0 and 'the choice' is greater than 6 then,
            Set 'write a method here' to true.
        If 'the fields left' is 0 then,
            Set 'write a method here' to true.
        a number called 'the entries after this' is 'how many entries' minus 'the entries written',
        a text called 'the ending' is ",",
        If 'the entries after this' is 1 then,
            Set 'the ending' to ".".
        a number called 'the entry' is 'the first field' add 'the field step',
        If 'write a method here' then,
            Set 'the entry' to 'the first method' add 'the method step',
            Set 'the method step' to 'the method step' add 1,
            Set 'the methods left' to 'the methods left' minus 1.
        If 'write a method here' is false then,
            Set 'the field step' to 'the field step' add 1,
            Set 'the fields left' to 'the fields left' minus 1.
        'gen emit one thing entry' of 'the entry' and 'write a method here' and 'the ending',
        Set 'the entries written' to 'the entries written' add 1.
    'gen emit' of "\n".
    Return a number, 0.

(One line of a thing's body: a manifest entry, or a data field with or
 without its default. LANGUAGE.md:967 says a field without a default
 takes its type's zero value, so both spellings are legal and which one
 a field gets is drawn; a nested thing and a time have no literal to
 default to and never carry one.)

To 'gen emit one thing entry' with a number called 'the entry' and a boolean called 'it is a method' and a text called 'the ending'.
    If 'it is a method' then,
        a text called 'the method name' is 'gen method written' of 'the entry',
        'gen emit' of "    a function called {'the method name'}{'the ending'}\n",
        Return a number, 0.
    a text called 'the field name' is 'gen field written' of 'the entry'.
    a text called 'the field type' is 'gen field type written' of 'the entry'.
    a text called 'the default' is 'gen field default written' of 'the entry'.
    a text called 'the field line' is "    a {'the field type'} called {'the field name'}{'the ending'}\n".
    If 'the default' is not "" then,
        Set 'the field line' to "    a {'the field type'} called {'the field name'} is {'the default'}{'the ending'}\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the field line'.
    Return a number, 0.

(A thing's members. Every declared member returns its owner
 (LANGUAGE.md:1454) and is defined exactly once (LANGUAGE.md:1513); a
 maker's first parameter is a number and a receiver's is the owner
 itself, which is what decides whether the type possessive alone reaches
 it or both call forms do.

 A thing whose fields are all floats, booleans, times or nested things
 has no number field to write, and then the body is just the declaration
 and the Return - still a legal member, verified against 0.4.7.)

To 'gen emit methods of' with a number called 'the thing'.
    a number called 'the first method' is element 'the thing' of gen_thing_method_first.
    a number called 'how many methods' is element 'the thing' of gen_thing_method_count.
    a number called 'the step' is 0.
    While 'the step' is less than 'how many methods',
        a number called 'the method' is 'the first method' add 'the step',
        'gen emit one method' of 'the thing' and 'the method',
        Set 'the step' to 'the step' add 1.
    Return a number, 0.

To 'gen emit one method' with a number called 'the thing' and a number called 'the method'.
    a text called 'the type' is 'gen thing written' of 'the thing'.
    a text called 'the type possessive' is 'gen thing possessive' of 'the thing'.
    a text called 'the method name' is 'gen method written' of 'the method'.
    a text called 'the parameter' is 'gen method param written' of 'the method'.
    a text called 'the parameter possessive' is 'gen method param possessive' of 'the method'.
    a text called 'the local' is 'gen method local written' of 'the method'.
    a text called 'the local possessive' is 'gen method local possessive' of 'the method'.
    a number called 'the kind' is element 'the method' of gen_method_kind.
    a number called 'the field' is element 'the method' of gen_method_field.
    a text called 'the parameter type' is "number".
    If 'the kind' is 1 then,
        Set 'the parameter type' to 'the type'.
    'gen emit' of "To do the {'the type possessive'} {'the method name'}, with a {'the parameter type'} called {'the parameter'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of "    a {'the type'} called {'the local'}.\n".
    If 'the field' is not 0 then,
        a text called 'the field name' is 'gen field written' of 'the field',
        a text called 'the written value' is 'the parameter',
        If 'the kind' is 1 then,
            Set 'the written value' to "0 subtract {'the parameter possessive'} {'the field name'}".
        'gen emit' of "    Set {'the local possessive'} {'the field name'} to {'the written value'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of "    Return a {'the type'}, {'the local'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of "\n".
    Return a number, 0.

( ── things leaves, batch A, 2026-08-28 ──

 THG-12, THG-25, THG-34, THG-37, THG-58, THG-64. Every leaf below defines
 its OWN fresh thing type(s) (and, for THG-58/64, a fresh plain function)
 rather than asking the manifest for one already built, because each row
 needs a SPECIFIC field-default shape the manifest's own random draw
 cannot guarantee on demand (an undefaulted field of a given kind, or a
 declared default the leaf must know in advance to assert against). A
 thing definition is legal only at the true top level (LANGUAGE.md:938,
 THG-03), so every leaf here is registered top-level-only in
 gen_core.vox's kind bands - hand-verified against vox 0.4.14 that a
 fresh `A thing called ...` and a fresh `To ...` may both be interleaved
 among a program's ordinary top-level statements, not only before them.

 Names are spent from the SAME vocabularies and cycle state the manifest
 itself uses (gen_type_words/gen_field_words/gen_function_words with
 their existing spent/offset/stride globals, gen_manifest.vox's own
 'gen fresh parameter phrase') rather than a new pool of this batch's
 own - 'gen cycled word' already guarantees no repeat within one program
 (it grows a disambiguating suffix once a vocabulary's own laps run out),
 and reusing the manifest's already-once-per-program-reset cycle state is
 what makes that guarantee apply here too, with no new reset to wire in.)

(A permutation of the field slots 0..3, so THG-12's four zero-typed
 fields are declared in no fixed order across draws - nothing in
 LANGUAGE.md pins field order and a generator that always wrote
 number/float/boolean/time in that sequence would be exactly the
 undeclared-invariant CLAUDE.md warns against.)

a list called gen_things_a_zero_field_order is [[0,1,2,3],[0,1,3,2],[0,2,1,3],[0,2,3,1],[0,3,1,2],[0,3,2,1],[1,0,2,3],[1,0,3,2],[1,2,0,3],[1,2,3,0],[1,3,0,2],[1,3,2,0],[2,0,1,3],[2,0,3,1],[2,1,0,3],[2,1,3,0],[2,3,0,1],[2,3,1,0],[3,0,1,2],[3,0,2,1],[3,1,0,2],[3,1,2,0],[3,2,0,1],[3,2,1,0]].

(The same, for THG-37's three pinned fields.)

a list called gen_things_a_pinned_field_order is [[0,1,2],[0,2,1],[1,0,2],[1,2,0],[2,0,1],[2,1,0]].

To 'gen things a kind keyword' with a number called kind.
    If kind is 0 then,
        Return a text, "number".
    If kind is 1 then,
        Return a text, "float".
    If kind is 2 then,
        Return a text, "boolean".
    Return a text, "time".

To 'gen things a boolean draw'.
    a number called 'the truth draw' is 'rng below' of 11.
    If 'the truth draw' is less than 6 then,
        Return a number, 0.
    Return a number, 1.

To 'gen things a boolean literal' with a number called truth.
    If truth is 0 then,
        Return a text, "false".
    Return a text, "true".

(A fresh, program-unique type/field/function phrase, spent from the
 manifest's own vocabulary and cycle state - see the block comment
 above.)

To 'gen things a fresh type'.
    Set gen_type_spent to gen_type_spent add 1.
    a text called 'the phrase' is 'gen cycled word' of gen_type_words and gen_type_spent and gen_type_offset and gen_type_stride.
    Return a text, 'the phrase'.

To 'gen things a fresh field'.
    Set gen_field_spent to gen_field_spent add 1.
    a text called 'the phrase' is 'gen cycled word' of gen_field_words and gen_field_spent and gen_field_offset and gen_field_stride.
    Return a text, 'the phrase'.

To 'gen things a fresh function'.
    Set gen_function_spent to gen_function_spent add 1.
    a text called 'the phrase' is 'gen cycled word' of gen_function_words and gen_function_spent and gen_function_offset and gen_function_stride.
    Return a text, 'the phrase'.

(THG-12: a field without a default takes its type's zero value -
 number 0, float 0.0, boolean 0, time 0 (LANGUAGE.md:967, 1055-1056). A
 fresh thing gets one undefaulted field of each of the four zero-having
 types, in a random order, and every field is read back before any write
 and asserted against the RENDERED zero the manual promises - hand-
 verified against vox 0.4.14 that `If sample's drift is not 0.0 then`
 both compiles and holds for a fresh, never-written float field, so the
 float assertion compares against the literal `0.0`, not the bare `0`
 that would be wrong for this type.)

To 'gen leaf thing zero default' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a text called 'the type phrase' is 'gen things a fresh type'.
    a text called 'the type' is 'gen written name' of 'the type phrase'.
    a text called 'number phrase' is 'gen things a fresh field'.
    a text called 'float phrase' is 'gen things a fresh field'.
    a text called 'boolean phrase' is 'gen things a fresh field'.
    a text called 'time phrase' is 'gen things a fresh field'.
    a text called 'number field' is 'gen written name' of 'number phrase'.
    a text called 'float field' is 'gen written name' of 'float phrase'.
    a text called 'boolean field' is 'gen written name' of 'boolean phrase'.
    a text called 'time field' is 'gen written name' of 'time phrase'.
    a list called 'the field names' is ['number field', 'float field', 'boolean field', 'time field'].
    a number called 'how many orders' is gen_things_a_zero_field_order's length.
    a number called 'the order draw' is 'rng below' of 'how many orders'.
    a number called 'the order slot' is 'the order draw' add 1.
    a list called 'the order' is element 'the order slot' of gen_things_a_zero_field_order.
    'gen emit' of "A thing called {'the type'} has\n".
    a number called 'the position' is 1.
    While 'the position' is less than or equal to 4,
        a number called 'the field kind' is element 'the position' of 'the order',
        a text called 'the field keyword' is 'gen things a kind keyword' of 'the field kind',
        a number called 'the name slot' is 'the field kind' add 1,
        a text called 'the field name' is element 'the name slot' of 'the field names',
        a text called 'the ending' is ",",
        If 'the position' is 4 then,
            Set 'the ending' to ".".
        'gen emit' of "    a {'the field keyword'} called {'the field name'}{'the ending'}\n",
        Set 'the position' to 'the position' add 1.
    'gen emit' of "\n".
    Set gen_instances to gen_instances add 1.
    a text called 'the instance declaration' is "a {'the type'} called i{gen_instances}".
    a text called 'number subject' is "i{gen_instances}'s {'number field'}".
    a text called 'float subject' is "i{gen_instances}'s {'float field'}".
    a text called 'boolean subject' is "i{gen_instances}'s {'boolean field'}".
    a text called 'time subject' is "i{gen_instances}'s {'time field'}".
    a text called 'number assert' is 'gen assert number is' of "THG-12" and 'number subject' and 0.
    a text called 'float assert' is 'gen assert number' of "THG-12" and 'float subject' and "0.0" and "0.0".
    a text called 'boolean assert' is 'gen assert false' of "THG-12" and 'boolean subject'.
    a text called 'time assert' is 'gen assert number is' of "THG-12" and 'time subject' and 0.
    a list called 'the lines' is ['the instance declaration', 'number assert', 'float assert', 'boolean assert', 'time assert'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(THG-37: a float field and a boolean field carry defaults; a number
 field with none is 0 (LANGUAGE.md:1055-1056) - the water-tank shape,
 field order and values random. Distinct from THG-12 above: here the
 float and boolean fields ALWAYS carry a declared default and the number
 field NEVER does, in one thing at once, matching the row's own wording
 rather than THG-12's all-undefaulted shape.)

To 'gen leaf thing pinned defaults' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a text called 'the type phrase' is 'gen things a fresh type'.
    a text called 'the type' is 'gen written name' of 'the type phrase'.
    a text called 'float phrase' is 'gen things a fresh field'.
    a text called 'boolean phrase' is 'gen things a fresh field'.
    a text called 'number phrase' is 'gen things a fresh field'.
