        a text called 'the target decl' is "a {'the type'} called i{'the target instance number'}",
        append 'the target decl' to 'the lines'.
    If 'the form draw' is 1 then,
        a text called 'the create decl' is "Create a {'the type'} called i{'the target instance number'}",
        append 'the create decl' to 'the lines'.
    If 'the form draw' is 2 then,
        a text called 'the source decl' is "a {'the type'} called i{'the target instance number'}",
        append 'the source decl' to 'the lines',
        Set gen_instances to gen_instances add 1,
        a number called 'the copy instance number' is gen_instances,
        a text called 'the copy decl' is "Set a {'the type'} called i{'the copy instance number'} to i{'the target instance number'}",
        append 'the copy decl' to 'the lines',
        Set 'the target instance number' to 'the copy instance number'.
    a number called 'the field checked so far' is 1.
    While 'the field checked so far' is less than or equal to 'how many fields',
        a text called 'the checked name' is element 'the field checked so far' of 'the field names',
        a text called 'the checked keyword' is element 'the field checked so far' of 'the field keywords',
        a text called 'the checked default' is element 'the field checked so far' of 'the field defaults',
        a text called 'the subject' is "i{'the target instance number'}'s {'the checked name'}",
        a text called 'the assert line' is 'gen assert number' of "THG-25" and 'the subject' and 'the checked default' and 'the checked default',
        If 'the checked keyword' is "boolean" and 'the checked default' is "true" then,
            Set 'the assert line' to 'gen assert true' of "THG-25" and 'the subject'.
        If 'the checked keyword' is "boolean" and 'the checked default' is "false" then,
            Set 'the assert line' to 'gen assert false' of "THG-25" and 'the subject'.
        append 'the assert line' to 'the lines',
        Set 'the field checked so far' to 'the field checked so far' add 1.
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(THG-58: a function receives a COPY of a thing (LANGUAGE.md:1199-1201).
 A fresh function takes a fresh thing type by value, writes its
 parameter's one number field, and returns it; the caller's own value is
 asserted UNCHANGED afterwards, and the returned copy is asserted
 mutated - the write cannot escape the call, and `Return` is the only
 way a change gets back to the caller (THG-59, exercised here too).)

