( ── things leaves, batch A, 2026-08-29 ──

 THG2-06, THG2-08, THG2-09, THG2-10, THG2-21, THG2-27, THG2-30, THG2-32,
 THG2-70: docs/ledger/things-b.md. A second, smaller manifest alongside
 gen_manifest.vox's, for the ordinary global functions and predicate
 function this batch's leaves need - built once per program the same
 "drawn whether or not it is used" way 'gen build manifest extras'
 builds the grid sink and flag reader, but living here because nothing
 outside this file needs to know about it.)

a boolean called gen_thing_function_ready is false.

a number called gen_thing_function_owner is 0.

a number called gen_thing_function_field is 0.

a text called gen_thing_function_squaring_written is "".

a text called gen_thing_function_scaling_written is "".

a boolean called gen_thing_function_nested_ready is false.

a number called gen_thing_function_outer_thing is 0.

a number called gen_thing_function_outer_field is 0.

a boolean called gen_thing_predicate_ready is false.

a text called gen_thing_predicate_written is "".

a list called gen_thing_call_prepositions is ["of", "to", "with", "on"].

(THG2-70 (LANGUAGE.md:1898-1900): the type nouns `is a <type>` recognises
 are the six builtins - number, text, decimal, boolean, list, map. One
 dispatch function, built once and unconditionally - even a program with
 zero things gets one, since it takes only a `value` and depends on
 nothing else on the page. Its branches are rotated and its float/
 decimal branch's spelling is drawn, reusing 'gen tag predicate' and
 'gen bare tag name' from gen_collections.vox rather than re-deriving
 VAL-03's own six-way split.)

To 'gen build thing predicate function'.
    Set gen_function_spent to gen_function_spent add 1.
    a text called 'the phrase' is 'gen cycled word' of gen_function_words and gen_function_spent and gen_function_offset and gen_function_stride.
    Set gen_thing_predicate_written to 'gen written name' of 'the phrase'.
    a text called 'the param phrase' is 'gen fresh parameter phrase'.
    a text called 'the param' is 'gen written name' of 'the param phrase'.
    'gen open a function definition'.
    'gen emit' of "To {gen_thing_predicate_written} with a value called {'the param'}.\n".
    a number called 'the rotation' is 'rng below' of 6.
    a number called 'the tag step' is 0.
    While 'the tag step' is less than 6,
        a number called 'the raw tag' is 'the tag step' add 'the rotation',
        a number called 'the tag' is 'the raw tag' modulo 6,
        a text called 'the predicate' is 'gen tag predicate' of 'the tag',
        a text called 'the label' is 'gen bare tag name' of 'the tag',
        a text called opener is "Otherwise if",
        If 'the tag step' is 0 then,
            Set opener to "If".
        'gen emit' of "    {opener} {'the param'} is {'the predicate'} then, Return a text, \"{'the label'}\".\n",
        Set 'the tag step' to 'the tag step' add 1.
    (Unreachable by any call this batch's leaves write - all six tags are
     covered above and none of the callers ever passes `nothing` - but
     still on the page in every program, so a fixed label here was a
     100%-present invariant with no citation (measured: the campaign
     that found it). Drawn from the field-word pool instead, the same
     one 'gen leaf thing format whole' already reads from.)
    a text called 'the fallback label' is 'gen word from' of gen_field_words.
    'gen emit' of "    Otherwise, Return a text, \"{'the fallback label'}\".\n".
    'gen emit' of "\n".
    Set gen_thing_predicate_ready to true.
    Return a number, 0.

(THG2-21, THG2-27, THG2-30, THG2-32 (LANGUAGE.md:1476-1480): a function
 computing some other type from a thing is an ordinary global function
 with no manifest entry, reached by the instance possessive - unlike
 every function 'gen emit prelude functions' already puts on the page
 (src/gen_core.vox:843-860), which take only numbers and texts. Two such
 functions, built once and unconditionally on the same thing:

 - the arity-one form (THG2-21): takes the thing, returns its chosen
   number field squared;
 - the arity-two form (THG2-27, THG2-30): takes the thing and a number,
   returns the field multiplied by it.

 Built around a NESTED thing's inner type when one exists, because that
 is the one shape THG2-32 (a receiver reached through a field) can also
 drive; a plain thing with a number field otherwise, which is all
 THG2-21/27/30 need. Names come out of the SAME function-name cycle
 'gen build manifest functions' spends from (gen_function_words, via the
 exposed gen_function_spent/offset/stride), so they can never collide
 with an ordinary manifest function - the same trick 'gen build manifest
 extras' uses for the grid sink and flag reader.)

To 'gen build thing functions'.
    Set gen_thing_function_ready to false.
    Set gen_thing_function_nested_ready to false.
    a boolean called 'a nesting is available' is 'gen manifest pick a nested thing'.
    If 'a nesting is available' then,
        Set gen_thing_function_owner to gen_pick_inner_thing,
        Set gen_thing_function_field to gen_pick_inner_field,
        Set gen_thing_function_nested_ready to true,
        Set gen_thing_function_outer_thing to gen_pick_thing,
        Set gen_thing_function_outer_field to gen_pick_field.
    a boolean called 'a plain thing is available' is false.
    If 'a nesting is available' is false then,
        Set 'a plain thing is available' to 'gen manifest pick a plain thing'.
    If 'a plain thing is available' then,
        Set gen_thing_function_owner to gen_pick_thing,
        Set gen_thing_function_field to gen_pick_field.
    a boolean called 'a thing is available' is false.
    If 'a nesting is available' then,
        Set 'a thing is available' to true.
    If 'a plain thing is available' then,
        Set 'a thing is available' to true.
    If 'a thing is available' is false then,
        Return a number, 0.
    Set gen_thing_function_ready to true.
    a text called 'the owner type' is 'gen thing written' of gen_thing_function_owner.
    a text called 'the field name' is 'gen field written' of gen_thing_function_field.
    Set gen_function_spent to gen_function_spent add 1.
    a text called 'the squaring phrase' is 'gen cycled word' of gen_function_words and gen_function_spent and gen_function_offset and gen_function_stride.
    Set gen_thing_function_squaring_written to 'gen written name' of 'the squaring phrase'.
    a text called 'the squaring parameter phrase' is 'gen fresh parameter phrase'.
    a text called 'the squaring parameter' is 'gen written name' of 'the squaring parameter phrase'.
    a text called 'the squaring parameter possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the squaring parameter phrase'.
    a text called 'the squaring introducer' is 'gen parameter introducer'.
    'gen open a function definition'.
    'gen emit' of "To {gen_thing_function_squaring_written} {'the squaring introducer'} a {'the owner type'} called {'the squaring parameter'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of "    Return a number, {'the squaring parameter possessive'} {'the field name'} multiply {'the squaring parameter possessive'} {'the field name'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of "\n".
    Set gen_function_spent to gen_function_spent add 1.
    a text called 'the scaling phrase' is 'gen cycled word' of gen_function_words and gen_function_spent and gen_function_offset and gen_function_stride.
    Set gen_thing_function_scaling_written to 'gen written name' of 'the scaling phrase'.
    a text called 'the scaling parameter phrase' is 'gen fresh parameter phrase'.
    a text called 'the scaling parameter' is 'gen written name' of 'the scaling parameter phrase'.
    a text called 'the scaling parameter possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the scaling parameter phrase'.
    a text called 'the factor phrase' is 'gen fresh parameter phrase'.
    a text called 'the factor parameter' is 'gen written name' of 'the factor phrase'.
    a text called 'the scaling introducer' is 'gen parameter introducer'.
    'gen open a function definition'.
    'gen emit' of "To {gen_thing_function_scaling_written} {'the scaling introducer'} a {'the owner type'} called {'the scaling parameter'} and a number called {'the factor parameter'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of "    Return a number, {'the scaling parameter possessive'} {'the field name'} multiply {'the factor parameter'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of "\n".
    Return a number, 0.

(Reused from gen_buffers.vox: 'gen assert number is'/'gen assert number
 matches' cover every numeric call-result assertion below (THG2-21,
 THG2-27, THG2-30, THG2-32). Two more of the same two-statement shape -
 an If that closes on its own period, then a plain Print to punctuate
 the join and keep the observed value in the corpus - for the two
 comparisons buffers never needed: thing equality (THG2-08, THG2-09,
 THG2-10) and text equality (THG2-70).)

To 'gen assert things equal' with a text called 'the row' and a text called 'the left' and a text called 'the right'.
    a text called 'the line' is "If {'the left'} is not {'the right'} then, Print \"ASSERT {'the row'}: expected {'the left'} to equal {'the right'}\", Exit 95. Print {'the left'}".
    Return a text, 'the line'.

To 'gen assert things not equal' with a text called 'the row' and a text called 'the left' and a text called 'the right'.
    a text called 'the line' is "If {'the left'} is {'the right'} then, Print \"ASSERT {'the row'}: expected {'the left'} to differ from {'the right'}\", Exit 95. Print {'the left'}".
    Return a text, 'the line'.

To 'gen assert text equals' with a text called 'the row' and a text called 'the subject' and a text called 'the expected'.
    a text called 'the got shown' is 'gen buffer slot of' of 'the subject'.
    a text called 'the line' is "If {'the subject'} is not \"{'the expected'}\" then, Print \"ASSERT {'the row'}: expected {'the expected'} got {'the got shown'}\", Exit 95. Print {'the subject'}".
    Return a text, 'the line'.

(THG2-06 (LANGUAGE.md:1357-1358): a whole thing interpolates into a
 format string under `Print`, the same rendering `Print p.` produces on
 its own - the existing leaves ('gen thing flat', 'gen thing nested')
 already put a bare `Print i{n}.` on the page; this is the first leaf to
 put the SAME instance inside a `{…}` slot instead. Not assertable from
 inside: neither rendering can be captured into a comparable value
 (THG2-01), and interpolating a whole thing into a TEXT initializer is
 rejected outright rather than merely uncheckable (LANGUAGE.md:1359-
 1362, "Interpolate a field instead"), so there is no route to a captured
 value even in principle. The two Prints below - the bare thing and the
 same instance inside a format string - are the whole of the check;
 agreeing with each other is the harness's job, not this program's.)

To 'gen leaf thing format whole' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a boolean called 'a thing is available' is 'gen manifest pick a plain thing'.
    If 'a thing is available' is false then,
        'gen manifest stand aside' of indent and nested,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a text called 'the type' is 'gen thing written' of gen_pick_thing.
    a text called 'the field' is 'gen field written' of gen_pick_field.
    Set gen_instances to gen_instances add 1.
    a text called 'the instance name' is "i{gen_instances}".
    a text called 'the instance declaration' is "a {'the type'} called {'the instance name'}".
    a list called 'the lines' is ['the instance declaration'].
    a number called 'the set draw' is 'rng below' of 3.
    If 'the set draw' is less than 2 then,
        a text called 'a literal' is 'literal integer',
        a text called 'the set line' is "Set {'the instance name'}'s {'the field'} to {'a literal'}",
        append 'the set line' to 'the lines'.
    a text called 'the bare print' is "Print {'the instance name'}".
    append 'the bare print' to 'the lines'.
    a text called 'the slot' is 'gen buffer slot of' of 'the instance name'.
    a text called 'a word' is 'gen word from' of gen_field_words.
    (Not "the {word} shows ..." - gen_field_words mixes bare words with
     phrases that already open on "the" ("the arc", "the gradient"), and
     prepending an article assuming the word has none produced "the the
     arc shows ..." for every phrase entry. This shape reads aloud
     whichever kind of word is drawn.)
    a text called 'the sentence' is "{'a word'} reading: {'the slot'}".
    a text called 'the interpolated print' is "Print \"{'the sentence'}\"".
    append 'the interpolated print' to 'the lines'.
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(THG2-08, THG2-09 (LANGUAGE.md:1376-1377): `is` between two values of
 the same thing compares those same fields at the same depth, and `is
 not` is its negation. Two fresh instances start equal by construction -
 every field takes its type's zero value until this leaf sets one - so
 the `is` check runs first with no Set at all; then the SAME field on
 the second instance is set to a value numerically distinct from that
 default (a redraw loop on the NUMBER rather than a "not 0" text guard,
 because a signed leading-zero literal like "-0" is textually not "0"
 while numerically holding the field's own default - a bare string
 compare would miss it and turn the not-equal assertion into a false
 finding), and `is not` runs on the pair it produced.)

To 'gen leaf thing equality' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a boolean called 'a thing is available' is 'gen manifest pick a plain thing'.
    If 'a thing is available' is false then,
        'gen manifest stand aside' of indent and nested,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a text called 'the type' is 'gen thing written' of gen_pick_thing.
    a text called 'the field' is 'gen field written' of gen_pick_field.
    Set gen_instances to gen_instances add 1.
    a text called 'the first name' is "i{gen_instances}".
    Set gen_instances to gen_instances add 1.
    a text called 'the second name' is "i{gen_instances}".
    a text called 'the first declaration' is "a {'the type'} called {'the first name'}".
    a text called 'the second declaration' is "a {'the type'} called {'the second name'}".
    a text called 'the equal assert' is 'gen assert things equal' of "THG2-08" and 'the first name' and 'the second name'.
    a text called 'the differing literal' is 'literal integer'.
    a number called 'the differing value' is 'the differing literal' as a number.
    While 'the differing value' is 0,
        Set 'the differing literal' to 'literal integer',
        Set 'the differing value' to 'the differing literal' as a number.
    a text called 'the set line' is "Set {'the second name'}'s {'the field'} to {'the differing literal'}".
    a text called 'the not equal assert' is 'gen assert things not equal' of "THG2-09" and 'the first name' and 'the second name'.
    a list called 'the lines' is ['the first declaration', 'the second declaration', 'the equal assert', 'the set line', 'the not equal assert'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(THG2-10 (LANGUAGE.md:1377-1378): the comparison is written out by the
 compiler, so it recurses into nested things - the difference this time
 sits two levels down, in the field of a field. Same construction as
 THG2-08/09: two fresh outer instances start equal (every field
 defaults, all the way down), diverge in the nested field, then converge
 back by setting the second to match the first's own drawn literal
 rather than to a second independent draw - two independent draws could
 coincide and silently stay unequal.)

