    Set gen_instances to gen_instances add 1.
    a text called 'the second name' is "i{gen_instances}".
    a text called 'the first declaration' is "a {'the outer type'} called {'the first name'}".
    a text called 'the second declaration' is "a {'the outer type'} called {'the second name'}".
    a text called 'the differing literal' is 'literal integer'.
    a number called 'the differing value' is 'the differing literal' as a number.
    While 'the differing value' is 0,
        Set 'the differing literal' to 'literal integer',
        Set 'the differing value' to 'the differing literal' as a number.
    a text called 'the diverge line' is "Set {'the first name'}'s {'the outer field possessive'} {'the inner field'} to {'the differing literal'}".
    a text called 'the not equal assert' is 'gen assert things not equal' of "THG2-10" and 'the first name' and 'the second name'.
    a text called 'the converge line' is "Set {'the second name'}'s {'the outer field possessive'} {'the inner field'} to {'the differing literal'}".
    a text called 'the equal assert' is 'gen assert things equal' of "THG2-10" and 'the first name' and 'the second name'.
    a list called 'the lines' is ['the first declaration', 'the second declaration', 'the diverge line', 'the not equal assert', 'the converge line', 'the equal assert'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(THG2-21 (LANGUAGE.md:1476-1480): a function computing some other type
 from a thing is an ordinary global function with no manifest entry,
 reached by BOTH the free call and the instance possessive - the two
 built once in 'gen build thing functions' and called here on a fresh
 instance, each result asserted against the field value the generator
 just wrote.)

