    Set gen_args to gen_args add 1.
    a text called 'the receiver result' is "c{gen_args}".
    a text called 'the receiver decl' is "a number called {'the receiver result'} is {'the instance name'}'s {gen_thing_function_squaring_written}".
    a text called 'the receiver assert' is 'gen assert number is' of "THG2-21" and 'the receiver result' and 'the expected'.
    a list called 'the lines' is ['the instance declaration', 'the set line', 'the free decl', 'the free assert', 'the receiver decl', 'the receiver assert'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(THG2-27 (LANGUAGE.md:1521): `of`, `to`, `with`, and `on` all introduce
 arguments - covered here in the free-call form, all four every firing
 (the row's own claim is that all four exist, so testing all four is the
 citation, not an invariant needing one); THG2-30 covers the instance-
 possessive form and the extra-argument-after-preposition rule
 specifically. Which spelling comes first is rotated, the same idiom
 'gen leaf value dispatch's branch order and 'gen cycled word' use, so
 the four are never in the same order twice running.)

To 'gen leaf thing call prepositions' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    If gen_thing_function_ready is false then,
        'gen manifest stand aside' of indent and nested,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a text called 'the type' is 'gen thing written' of gen_thing_function_owner.
    a text called 'the field' is 'gen field written' of gen_thing_function_field.
