(THG2-70 (LANGUAGE.md:1898-1900): calls 'gen build thing predicate
 function's dispatch with a drawn payload of one of the six builtin tags
 (number/text/decimal-or-float/boolean/list/map, reusing 'gen value
 payload'/'gen value expression' from gen_collections.vox - VAL-03's own
 machinery for building one), asserting the branch that fired against
 the tag the generator drew. One call per firing rather than all six -
 the six-branch dispatch itself is already built once, unconditionally,
 regardless of which tag any single firing goes on to exercise, so a
 campaign's many firings put every branch on trial across the corpus.)

